      "challengedBy": [],
      "claim": "`parseRefreshTokenResponse` now returns the Zod `safeParse` wrapper, but the Google Calendar refresh path writes that wrapper directly into `credential.key`. The downstream Google credential parser expects a raw token object, so the persisted value no longer contains the fields that consumer reads (`access_token`, `expiry_date`, `refresh_token`). This causes the refresh credential shape to fail to round-trip through storage. Also observed in: packages/app-store/googlecalendar/lib/CalendarService.ts",
